# The reference-interpreter pairing (r01 criteria row 7): the lupin
# release this wolf is differentially tested against, and the
# conformance pin that lupin release itself declares.
#
# `wolf --version` prints this file; nothing else defines the pairing
# (#87 retired the hardcoded constants that went three releases stale).
# Update it WITH the differential ritual — the pairing test compares
# the version below against the sibling lupin binary whenever one is
# present (and, when that sibling is a release build, the pin too:
# D57, a release's pin is part of its identity), so a stale stamp
# fails the local gauntlet instead of shipping.
#
# The ritual has a CONTROL step (#281), and it is not optional: after
# measuring the corpus against the NEW interpreter, measure the same
# corpus, same tree, same `wolf`, against the PREVIOUS stamp's release
# archive and diff the two ledgers. Without it every count that moved
# gets attributed to the interpreter by default, which at r13 would
# have been wrong seven times over. One command:
#
#   cargo xtask differ target/release/wolf <new-lupin> --triage --checked \
#       --control <previous-lupin-or-.tar.gz>
#
# (and again with --native). It prints "the interpreter bump moved N
# counts" with N measured, names the files, and reports the moves that
# live BELOW the ledger — a differing stdout on an unseeded file never
# reaches a count, and that is where r13's real interpreter delta was.
lupin-version = 0.1.32
lupin-pin = e0ce018
